title: $:/plugins/nikorion/table/language/en-GB/Playground/

Intro: Live examples of the `<<table>>` macro on the three `Demo Task` tiddlers. Every label, tooltip, status and date format follows the wiki language: switch it in the control panel to see the tables change. Each table gets its own `stateTiddler`, so their edit mode, sorting and pagination stay independent.
Basic/Heading: Basic table
Basic/Intro: Read-only view: click a column header to sort, click it again to reverse the order. `tags` is shown as is, other built-in columns get a localised header.
Editable/Heading: Editable, with actions and pagination
Editable/Intro: Click the pencil in the caption to toggle edit mode: inline editing, checkbox (marks a task ''Done''), clone and delete columns. The arrow column expands a record to show its text. The column currently used for sorting stays locked in edit mode.
Editable/Caption: Demo tasks
Footer/Heading: Numerical summary footer
Footer/Intro: `footerRows:"2"` adds two footer rows. In edit mode each footer cell is a text box whose wikitext is rendered in view mode, within the current column: type `<<sum>>`, `<<average 1>>`, `<<count>>`, `<<median>>`, `<<product>>`, `<<minall>>` or `<<maxall>>` (optional argument = number of decimal places). The cells below are pre-filled in `$:/keepstate/nikorion/table/Playground/footer/footer`.
Footer/Sum: Sum
Footer/Average: Average
